    <sys:String x:Key="Main_KillTimerHelpTitle">Remote desktop session</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Main_KillTimerHelpBody">While on, the launcher watches the mihomo VPN engine: whenever the engine is running, a 60-second countdown runs, and at zero the engine is stopped and the countdown restarts.&#10;&#10;Useful for remote setup (RDP, AnyDesk): if a wrong VPN config cuts your connection, access returns within 60 seconds.&#10;&#10;Turn it on during remote setup, off when done. Off by default.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Set_SafeModeHint">Stops mihomo every 60s while the engine is running, so you don't lose remote access.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Set_FirewallLabel">Block programs through Windows when the tunnel is unavailable</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Set_FirewallHint">The kill-switch inside the engine only works while the engine is alive. This protection lives in the Windows Firewall: programs from kill-switch rules cannot reach the internet around the tunnel — even if the engine crashed, is restarting, or the launcher is closed. The local network, printers and Remote Desktop are never affected.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Set_FirewallOff">Protection is off: if the engine stops, the programs go straight out.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Set_FirewallNeedsSetup">Setup needed: press "Set up mihomo" — it registers the task that creates the firewall rules (one UAC prompt).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Set_FirewallActive">Protection active: {0} rules in the firewall.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Set_FirewallNoPrograms">Nothing to protect: no kill-switch rule lists a program. The firewall cannot cover sites or templates — add the program that opens them to the rule.</sys:String>
