    <sys:String x:Key="Set_DnsSourceSub">From subscription «{0}»: {1}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Set_DnsDesc">Only for what bypasses the VPN and goes direct: everything not on a tile, tiles that are off, and whatever subscriptions send direct themselves. VPN traffic is resolved on the VPN server's side — this DNS never touches it and cannot hold it up. With the «Everything else» tile on, almost nothing goes direct, so this DNS is barely used.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Set_DnsPrimary">Primary</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Set_DnsSecondary">Secondary</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Set_DnsPlaceholder">Paste anything: 1.1.1.1 · https://dns.nextdns.io/abc123 · tls://dns.google · quic://… · sdns://…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Set_DnsPlaceholder2">Second address, e.g. 1.0.0.1</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Set_DnsTest">Test</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Set_DnsTesting">Testing — asking each server exactly the way the engine will…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Set_DnsNothingToTest">Enter a DNS address first.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Set_DnsFormats">The format is detected automatically: plain IP (then two lines — primary and secondary), IPv6, DoT (tls:// or just a server name), DoH (https://…, HTTP/2), DoH3 (h3:// or #h3=true — HTTP/3 over QUIC), DoQ (quic://), TCP (tcp://), sdns:// DNS stamps, a NextDNS profile ID (6 characters).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Set_DnsDirectNow">What goes direct right now — and will be resolved by this DNS</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Set_DnsJournalHint">To check one particular site, use the log («What was blocked and why»): its search line shows which rule it follows, direct or via VPN, and who resolves its name.</sys:String>
